phi-adapter-sdk (0.9.0-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * createLoopExecutionBackend(): the Qt-free instance execution backend.
    One named thread, one phi::runtime::EpollLoop, adapter callbacks one at
    a time in submission order - what sdk::qt::createInstanceExecutionBackend
    did, without libQt6Core. What the default backend could not do is the
    point of it: inside a callback, phi::runtime::Loop::current() is that
    thread's loop, so an adapter arms its own timers and watches its own
    descriptors. Having no way to do that is why adapters reached for QTimer
    and pulled QtCore onto the box behind it.
  * Stop stays bounded. A callback that will not return is handed to the
    abandoned-thread registry exactly as the default backend hands one over
    (F-35), so one wedged instance cannot hold a sidecar's teardown open.
  * The registry moved from sidecar.cpp into abandoned_threads.h now that two
    backends hand threads to it.
  * Builds against libphi-runtime.

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Mon, 08 Sep 2026 10:05:00 +0200

